course: dictionary
lesson: 9981
title: Teasing: friendly or hurtful?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Teasing means making fun of someone, or annoying them with words or tricks. Sometimes it is friendly and both people laugh. Sometimes it is hurtful and the other person feels sad. Look at the context to tell which one it is. «Not reacting can make a teasing game boring» suggests a game that both people can end, not one that hurts.
explain: «When Ben called his uncle a name after his uncle teased him, Dad sent Ben to the car for five minutes.» The teasing started it, but calling a name back did not make things better. Then Ben came back and said sorry, and his uncle said sorry too for the teasing. The clues show that hurtful teasing can hurt, and that both people can say sorry.
explain: Teasing can also be a verb, from tease, and an adjective, as in a teasing smile. The adjective describes a look or voice that is playful, not cruel. Ask yourself: is it gentle, or does it make someone sad? That question is the best check.
explain: If teasing hurts you, you do not have to deal with it alone. Tell the person to stop, and if it continues, tell an adult. Telling an adult is the proper way to stop it.
fact: Teasing means making fun of someone or annoying them with words or tricks.
fact: Friendly teasing is gentle, and both people laugh; hurtful teasing about looks, names or families makes someone sad.
fact: If teasing hurts, tell the person to stop, and tell an adult.
fact: Teasing can also mean playfully trying to make an animal or person want something, such as waving food at a pet.
fact: Teasing animals, like pulling their tails, can make them bite.
exercise: Ben's uncle teased him. What does teasing mean? | Giving someone a present | Running very fast | Singing a long song | *Making fun of someone or annoying them
exercise: Which kind of teasing is gentle and makes both people laugh? | Bullying | Pulling an animal's tail | Hurtful teasing about someone's family | *Friendly teasing
exercise: Ella asks what to do if teasing hurts her. What is the best answer? | Laugh along and say nothing ever | Tell no one at all | Tease them back harder | *Tell the person to stop and tell an adult
test: «Not reacting can make a teasing game boring; telling an adult stops it properly.» What does this suggest about hurtful teasing? | It is always funny | Ignoring it always ends it | *Telling an adult is the proper way to stop it | Teasing back is the best choice
test: Which action is teasing an animal? | Walking a dog on a lead | *Waving food at a dog to make it want it | Stroking a cat slowly | Feeding a fish at the pond
exam: What does teasing mean? | Being quiet in class | Painting pictures in art | Running a race | *Making fun of someone or annoying them with words or tricks
